>> title: Shakshuka
>> category: Eggs
>> tags: eggs, tomatoes, peppers, one-pot, skillet, breakfast
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: shakshouka, chakchouka, eggs in purgatory, eggs poached in tomato sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the sauce has to hold a spoon track before a single egg is cracked, or the whites run and you have tomato soup with egg in it
>> step.1: The eggs poach in the sauce they are served in, which is why this is one pan and not three.
>> step.2: soften 10 min
>> step.3: toast the spices 1 min
>> step.4: simmer 15 min, until it holds a spoon track
>> step.5: poach covered 8 min, whites set, yolks loose
>> step.6: Bread, not a plate. Serve it in the skillet on a board — lifted onto plates it arrives cold and broken.

The eggs poach in the sauce they are served in, which is the whole reason this is one pan and not three.

Soften @red bell peppers{2%large}(sliced in strips), @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced) in @olive oil{3%Tbs} in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~saute{10%min}.

Toast @&(~1)peppers{} with @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced), @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @sweet paprika{2%tsp}, @caraway seeds{1/2%tsp}(crushed), @harissa{1%Tbs} for ~toast{1%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)base{} with @canned whole tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g; crushed by hand), @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}, @sugar{1/2%tsp} for ~simmer{15%min}.

Poach @eggs{6} in wells pressed into @&(~1)sauce{} covered for ~poach{8%min} with @feta{4%oz}(115 g; crumbled), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Bread, not a plate, is how this leaves the pan.
